    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Beautifully Presented Detached Home in a Prime City Centre Setting!\r\n\r\nNo. 10 Coote's Lane is a modern detached two-storey residence extending approximately 92 sq. m. (990 sq. ft.) situated in a mature residential area, just off Upper Patrick Street and within easy walking distance of Kilkenny City Centre.\r\n\r\nConstructed in c. 2008 using traditional concrete block construction, the property offers a practical and well-balanced layout that makes excellent use of the available floor space. Bright, comfortable accommodation includes three bedrooms, three bathrooms, a spacious kitchen/dining room, separate utility room and a well-proportioned living room. It is also alarmed throughout. \r\n\r\nThe property has been upgraded in recent years to achieve a B3 energy rating, including pumped cavity wall insulation, additional attic insulation and thermostatic heating controls on both the ground and first floors, enhancing overall energy efficiency and comfort.\r\n\r\nThe property has been carefully maintained and is presented in excellent decorative condition throughout. Outside, it benefits from private off-street parking, gated side pedestrian access and an enclosed south-facing rear, combining the convenience of city living with the privacy of a well-established residential setting.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall\r\nA welcoming entrance hall with timber flooring provides access to the principal accommodation and sets the tone for the quality of finish found throughout the home.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nPositioned to the front of the property, the living room is a bright, well-proportioned reception room with wooden floor is centred around an attractive feature fireplace. A large front-facing window provides excellent natural light, creating a comfortable space for everyday living and entertaining.\r\n\r\nGuest W.C.\r\nA guest W.C., with window, is conveniently located on the ground floor.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining Room\r\nExtending across the rear of the property, the open-plan kitchen and dining room forms the heart of the home. The kitchen is fitted with contemporary high-gloss wall and floor units, polished tiled flooring and integrated appliances, offering generous storage and preparation space. The dining area comfortably accommodates family dining and social occasions.\r\n\r\nFrench doors open directly onto the south-facing rear patio area, providing an easy connection between the indoor and outdoor living spaces.\r\n\r\nUtility Room\r\nLocated just off the kitchen, the separate utility room is fitted with a side window, additional storage units and plumbing for laundry appliances. \r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nThe landing benefits from both roof and wall-mounted Velux windows, allowing natural light to filter through the centre of the home. A Stira folding attic stairs gives access to the floored attic making it an ideal storage space. \r\n\r\nPrincipal Bedroom \r\nA generous double bedroom positioned to the front of the property with fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nEnsuite Shower Room\r\nThe ensuite comprises a shower cubicle, wash hand basin, W.C. and window.\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nThe family bathroom comprises a bath, wash hand basin, W.C. and window.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two\r\nA comfortable single bedroom, with built in wardrobes, suitable as a child's bedroom, guest room or home office.\r\n\r\nBedroom Three\r\nA spacious double bedroom overlooking the rear garden with fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nTo the front, a cobble lock, walled, driveway provides valuable private off-street parking for two cars.\r\n\r\nA gated pedestrian entrance to the side of the property provides direct access to the enclosed, low maintenance, rear without the need to pass through the house.\r\n\r\nThe south-facing rear has been designed for ease of maintenance, with decorative paving and established planting creating an attractive and private outdoor space. It provides an ideal setting for outdoor dining, entertaining or simply relaxing.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nNo. 10 Coote's Lane enjoys an exceptionally convenient location just off Upper Patrick Street, placing a wide range of everyday amenities within easy reach.\r\n\r\nHigh Street, Market Cross Shopping Centre, cafés, restaurants, supermarkets, pharmacies and a variety of independent retailers are all within a short walk. \r\n\r\nThe property is immediately adjacent to De La Salle Boys' National School and St. John of God National School, while St. Kieran's College, Presentation Secondary School, Gaelscoil Osrai and a number of childcare facilities are also close by. \r\n\r\nA short stroll down Coote’s Lane will take you to Hotel Kilkenny with its leisure centre, spa, restaurant and bar, and further to the recently completed Rose Hill pedestrian Bridge, which links the area to the city ring road and surrounding walking and cycling routes. \r\n\r\nKilkenny Castle, the Parade, the Medieval Mile and a range of sporting and recreational amenities are also easily accessible, making this an ideal location for those seeking the convenience of city living.\r\n\r\nA Home That Offers Lifestyle as Well as Location!\r\n\r\nOne of the principal attractions of No. 10 Coote's Lane is the balance it offers between comfortable modern living and an exceptionally convenient location.\r\n\r\nThe practical layout, three bathrooms, private parking and south-facing rear combine to create a home suited to a wide range of purchasers. Equally important is its proximity to schools, shopping, cafés, restaurants and everyday services, allowing many daily journeys to be made on foot.\r\n\r\nPresented in excellent decorative condition throughout, No. 10 represents an opportunity to acquire a quality detached home in one of Kilkenny City's most established residential locations.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\n•\tDetached two-storey residence \r\n•\tApprox. 92 sq.m. (990 sq.ft.) \r\n•\tBuilt c. 2008 \r\n•\tTraditional concrete block construction \r\n•\tBER: B3\r\n•\tGas-fired central heating \r\n•\tThree bedrooms \r\n•\tThree bathrooms (guest W.C., family bathroom & ensuite) \r\n•\tWell-proportioned living room with feature fireplace \r\n•\tSpacious open-plan kitchen / dining room \r\n•\tSeparate utility room \r\n•\tPrivate off-street parking for two cars\r\n•\tGated side pedestrian access \r\n•\tEnclosed south-facing, low-maintenance, rear \r\n•\tDouble glazed uPVC windows \r\n•\tMains water and mains drainage \r\n•\tExcellent decorative condition throughout \r\n•\tWalking distance to Kilkenny City Centre \r\n•\tA bright, airy house with lots of windows\r\n•\tAlarmed throughout\r\n•\tThermostats fitted on the ground floor and first floor\r\n•\tAdditional insulation to include walls being pumped and additional attic insulation\r\n•\tA Stira folding attic stairs leads to generous, floored attic space\r\n\r\nDirections\r\nFrom The Parade, proceed straight along Patrick Street, passing The Left Bank, The Hibernian, Zuni, The Pembroke Hotel, Butler House, The Blue Bar etc., onto Upper Patrick Street. At the bend in the road, at The Village Inn, turn right onto Coote's Lane. No. 10 is located down the lane on the left-hand side and is identified by our For Sale sign. Eircode: R95 HT9E.\r\n\r\nViewing\r\nViewing is strictly by prior appointment with the sole selling agent, Warren McCreery. Please telephone (056) 770 2000 or see www.warrenmccreery.ie.\r\n\r\nThese particulars are issued strictly on the understanding that they do not form part of any contract and are provided, without liability, as a general guide only to what is being offered subject to contract and availability. They are not to be construed as containing any representation of fact upon which any interested party is entitled to rely. Any intending purchaser or lessee should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the accuracy of these particulars. The vendor or lessor do not make, give or imply nor is Warren McCreery or its staff authorized to make, give or imply any representation or warranty whatsoever in respect of this property. No responsibility can be accepted for any expenses incurred by intending purchasers in inspecting properties which have been sold let or withdrawn."
      },
